      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: If `k_poll` returns `-EAGAIN` (e.g. because of a timeout or `K_NO_WAIT`), but `events` actually picked up a matching event from `atomic_set()`, this logic will still unconditionally add `TASK_EVENT_TIMER` and break.\n\nTo prevent returning a timer event when a matching event was successfully retrieved, consider grouping the `rv \u003d\u003d -EAGAIN` check so it only applies when no matching events were found:\n```c\n\t\tif (!(event_mask \u0026 events) \u0026\u0026\n\t\t    (rv \u003d\u003d -EAGAIN || (timeout_us !\u003d -1 \u0026\u0026 ticks_left \u003c\u003d 0))) {\n```",
